  <DataNode TextLabel="XL VLDL" GraphId="baa03" Type="Pathway" GroupRef="aa467">
    <Comment>A triglyceride-rich lipoprotein particle that is typically composed of APOB100, APOE and APOCs and has a density of about 1.006 g/ml and a diameter of between 20-80 nm. It is found in blood and transports endogenous products (newly synthesized cholesterol and triglycerides) from the liver.</Comment>
